# Implementation Plan: QWebEngine Baseline Migration to `stable-integration`

> **Baseline Reference**: Golden Baseline Commit `1494056562065ceab04cea2475d6b9302dd69241` (Branch: `restore`)  
> **Target Branch**: `stable-integration` (New branch branched directly from `1494056`)  
> **Primary Directive**: Preserve the verified, in-process **`QWebEngineView`** browser engine and native Google/ChatGPT authentication flow while selectively porting independent features added after `1494056`.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Zero CDP / External Chrome Compromise**: The working `QWebEngineView` browser stack is the highest-priority constraint. All Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP) modules (`chrome_process.py`, `cdp_client.py`, screencast JPEG renderers, `--remote-debugging-port=9222`, and `AutomationControlled` flags) will be **EXCLUDED** from this migration.

> [!NOTE]
> The isolated/private clipboard experiment (`src/platform/private_clipboard.py`) was deleted in `main` (`e7df7cc`). The baseline `restore` clipboard architecture (`ClipboardMonitor` + SQLite repository) will remain intact.

